# herdr-lazy bundle — your declarative plugin set.
# One `owner/repo` per line. `#` starts a comment.
# Curated defaults below; edit to taste, then run `herdr-lazy sync`.

natori-hrj/herdr-lazy
cloudmanic/herdr-plus
persiyanov/herdr-reviewr
qu8n/herdr-automatic-rename

# Runs its TypeScript sources directly, so package.json declares
# `engines: node >= 23`. Declared regardless — this list is what the config
# recommends, not what a given machine can run.
AVGVSTVS96/herdr-drovr

# Considered for session management and not added:
#
#   andrewchng/herdr-sessionizer   [[build]] bun install
#   fullerzz/herdr-plugin-sesh     [[build]] go build
#   thanhdat77/herdr-navigator     [[build]] cargo build --release
#   yuk1ty/herdr-spreader          [[build]] cargo build --release
#   nikok6/herdr-mirror            prebuilt binary, but wants the preview
#                                  channel at both ends, and ssh or docker
#
# Each of the first four adds a toolchain to the install floor, and three of
# them map "session" onto a herdr *workspace*, which projects and `bellwethr
# save` already cover. None manages a herdr session, which is a whole server:
# a plugin runs inside one, and herdr refuses to attach from inside a pane.
